id: "E719"
trigger_tool: "conan|make|sh"
phase: "testing"
error_signature: "grep 65535|grep 4294967295|is not a valid positive integer, will use \\[0\\]|[0-9] of [0-9] tests failed"
severity: !!int "3"
category: "upstream-test-known-broken"
match_keywords: "opt 3.19, checkopt, USHORT error, ULONG error, opt_atou, atof, undefined behavior, fcvtzu, aarch64 saturation, 32-bit assumption, 4294967295, 65535, whitelist gate, known upstream failure, dh_auto_test || true, Debian rules, two-stage cross-check, HMBS_UPSTREAM_TEST_RESULT"
title: "Upstream assertions that can never pass on 64-bit OHOS ((unsigned long)atof(-1) is UB and aarch64 fcvtzu saturates to 0, and 4294967295 hardcodes 32-bit long) must not be edited to pass — gate them with a known-failure whitelist, per-TEST rc archiving and two-stage make-check cross-checking"
root_cause: "opt_atou() computes x = (unsigned long)atof(s); converting the negative double -1.0 to unsigned long is undefined behaviour, aarch64's fcvtzu saturates it to 0 (x86-64 would wrap), and the upstream expectation 4294967295 = 2^32-1 hardcodes a 32-bit unsigned long so no 64-bit platform can ever print it. Editing the assertions would be test-tuning; Debian's own opt_3.19-4 debian/rules tolerates the identical failures with 'dh_auto_test || true'."
affected_scope: "Any pre-2005 C test suite with word-size assumptions or UB-based conversions running on aarch64 OHOS; any recipe that would otherwise be tempted to weaken upstream assertions or to report make-check failure as PASS."
verification_cmd: "sh -c 't=\"$HOME/tmp/opt-3.19/w0/probe3/b/test/testtypes\"; \"$t\" -n -1; \"$t\" -o -1'"
rec_priority: !!int "1"
rec_approach: "known-failure-whitelist-gate-with-two-stage-cross-check"
rec_description: "Run each automake TEST individually with '{ cmd; rc=$?; echo HMBS_TEST_RC name=$rc; exit $rc; } > log 2>&1' and read the rc back from the log (missing rc = judge evidence missing -> raise). Then run 'make check' for the framework PASS:/FAIL: view and require both stages to agree. Count assertions with make-noise lines stripped ('make: ... is up to date.' contains dots) and treat '^Error: ' lines as failed assertions. Gate: failures must be a subset of the known broken set {USHORT error, ULONG error}, only checkopt may be non-zero, all three TESTs must be present; anything else raises ConanException. Emit HMBS_UPSTREAM_TEST_RESULT with the real failed count and report the real pass rate in notes and the PR body — never edit the assertions, never edit the library, never write PASS."
rec_command: "grep -E '^(PASS|FAIL):|HMBS_UPSTREAM_TEST_RESULT' <build>/make-check.log <build>/upstream-*.log"
rec_auto_fix: !!bool "false"
